# Central playground credentials — one local file for every Krokedil plugin.
#
# Copy this to ~/.config/krokedil-playground/.env (or merge the entries you
# are missing into your existing file) and fill in what you need; leave the
# rest commented out. Every plugin checkout and worktree reads it — a plugin's
# own gitignored .env overrides it per repo, and ambient env (shell exports,
# CI secrets) wins over everything.
#
# `krokedil-playground credentials` (run in a plugin repo) appends stubs for
# any names that plugin's playground.config.mjs reads but this file lacks.
#
# Sandbox/test credentials only — resolved values land in generated blueprints
# and throwaway playground sites, never use production keys.
#
# Onboarding a plugin? Add its credential names (with a comment saying where
# to obtain them) to this file via PR — see docs/onboarding.md.

# --- krokedil-playground tooling (--tunnel) ---
# Personal authtoken under the Krokedil ngrok pay-as-you-go account
# (dashboard.ngrok.com → Your Authtoken).
# NGROK_AUTHTOKEN=
# One tunnel wp-login password you know, reused across every playground
# (otherwise each --tunnel run prints a random one).
# KROKEDIL_PG_TUNNEL_PASS=
